# Entering the directory activates the flake's devshell: JDK 21, sbt, scalafmt
# and the Sail server, without typing `nix develop` every time. With nix-direnv
# the evaluated shell is cached, so entering is instant and nothing is rebuilt
# on each `cd`.
#
# This matters more than it looks for the IDE: IntelliJ inherits the environment
# of the terminal it was launched from. Opened from outside, it picks up
# SDKMAN's JAVA_HOME (a JDK 11) and Spark 4 does not even compile; opened from
# here with `idea .`, it picks up the flake's jdk21. The Direnv plugin for
# IntelliJ does the same job.
use flake

# The flake reads versions.json at evaluation time (Scala, Spark and pysail all
# come from there), but nix-direnv only watches flake.nix and flake.lock.
# Without this, bumping a version would not reload the shell and the Sail venv
# would stay on the previous one.
watch_file versions.json
